    silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensForgeRoutingFunctor is The routing functor R: F_04 to Backend that sends each typed source leg to a backend write target while preserving the leg's Yoneda profile (incoming and outgoing arrows). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'RoutingFunctor', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_03_materialization_spine_sections_01_interpret_step_decomposition_step_1__step_forge_morphism_for_01_interpret_step
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "CitedSource is a source object that has passed ingestion (it has a citation key and a source-boundary declaration). Spec is the schema-level commitment derived from it: a typed node in F_04 declaring the structure a Forge output must instantiate. interpret is the morphism connecting them." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_03_materialization_spine_sections_01_interpret_step_decomposition_step_2__step_forge_morphism_for_01_interpret_step
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The morphism interpret is an olog functor: it maps the CitedSource object to a Spec object while preserving the source-boundary declaration as a constraint. Functoriality: if S1 is a sub-witness of S2, the interpretation of S1 must factor through the interpretation of S2." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_03_materialization_spine_sections_01_interpret_step_decomposition_step_3__step_forge_morphism_for_01_interpret_step
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Every box maps to a box, every arrow maps to an arrow, every diagram law is preserved. From Spivak and Kent 2012." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_03_materialization_spine_sections_01_interpret_step_decomposition_step_4__step_forge_morphism_for_01_interpret_step
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
