    silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensVetRecordBackendTarget is The backend write target: the storage row where the typed measurement claim lands after routing — the row carries source key, value, date, observer, gate status. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'BackendTarget', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_03_materialization_spine_sections_02_render_step_decomposition_step_1__step_forge_morphism_for_02_render_step
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Spec is the schema-level commitment (domain). Template is the rendering process as a named olog object (codomain). render is the typed arrow in F_04 connecting them." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_03_materialization_spine_sections_02_render_step_decomposition_step_2__step_forge_morphism_for_02_render_step
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "render is not free-form code execution. It is a morphism in the Forge olog: every spec must be rendered by a declared template, and every template must carry (1) name, (2) version, (3) admitted spec types, (4) emitted artifact types." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_03_materialization_spine_sections_02_render_step_decomposition_step_3__step_forge_morphism_for_02_render_step
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "From Spivak and Kent 2012, every arrow in an olog is typed by its domain and codomain sentences. The template object inherits its typing from the spec it renders." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_03_materialization_spine_sections_02_render_step_decomposition_step_4__step_forge_morphism_for_02_render_step
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
