    rdfs:label "The mediator u is unique and determined by the universal property of the colimit. It is not freely chosen: if the candidate apex P receives the legs compatibly, the gate produces exactly one u." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_01_gate_discipline_sections_04_cocone_compatibility_decomposition_step_3__step_forge_morphism_for_04_cocone_compatibility
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Universal properties of colimits from category theory — limits and colimits in locally small categories." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_01_gate_discipline_sections_04_cocone_compatibility_decomposition_step_4__step_forge_morphism_for_04_cocone_compatibility
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "The Mittens diagram has seven typed source legs. A candidate apex P is admitted as Mittens only when ALL seven legs send compatible arrows to P." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_01_gate_discipline_sections_04_cocone_compatibility_decomposition_step_5__step_forge_morphism_for_04_cocone_compatibility
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By the Yoneda lemma, the colimit is determined up to unique isomorphism by its Hom-profile. The compatibility condition is the formal statement that the Yoneda embedding preserves this colimit: every leg's representation in the Hom-set must agree with the universal cocone maps." .

silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_01_gate_discipline_sections_04_cocone_compatibility_decomposition_step_6__step_forge_morphism_for_04_cocone_compatibility
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Cocone compatibility is the gate's final check: only a compatible cocone produces an admitted apex; fluency or partial coverage does not suffice." .

